' Historical behavior at the recorded baseline: Java wire path and response still use agent_id and session_id.
' Observed behavior: settings chooses a default model candidate and the model manager validates it.
' Historical behavior at the recorded baseline: Java accepts agent_ plus 24 alphanumeric characters and persists thinking false.
' Observed behavior: RandomSessionIdGenerator.nextId returns 26 Crockford Base32 characters with no prefix.
' Architecture change: target Agent and Session IDs use a type prefix plus 32 hex UUID characters.
' Architecture change: target HTTP path and payload fields use lowerCamelCase while header names stay unchanged.
' Product constraint: successful target creation persists thinking true.
' Header evidence: pi-mono-java 53eff85c7f41de23eb434e027782f5085a8b8e45, modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/web/RuntimeSessionController.java :: create; only request language is used.
' Observed behavior: creation persists an idle Session and does not initialize AgentSession or invoke a model.
' Architecture change: the materialized Session starts with zero lifetime Usage.
' Design reason: defer expensive runtime initialization until the first accepted user event.


actor "mate-service bridge" as Mate
participant "Session Controller" as API
participant "Session Service" as Service
participant "Agent directory resolver" as Resolver
participant "Model Manager" as Models
database "Session Repository" as Store

== Validate the published configuration ==
Mate -> API : POST /agents/{agentId}/sessions\noptional Accept-Language; no body
API -> API : validate typed agentId
API -> Service : create(agentId)
Service -> Resolver : resolve(agentId)
Resolver -> Resolver : validate controlled directory\nand published settings
Resolver --> Service : immutable configuration snapshot
Service -> Service : validate prompt availability\nand initial mode capability
Service -> Models : resolveDefaultModel(snapshot)
Models --> Service : validated default model

== Commit an idle resource ==
Service -> Service : allocate sessionId; build Session DTO
Service -> Store : create(idle, thinking=true, mode,\nversion=1, zero lifetimeUsage)
Store --> Service : committed Session
Service --> API : response VO from committed snapshot
API -> API : wrap with ResultBeanAdapter
API --> Mate : 201 + Location\nResultBean with Session resource

note over Service,Store
  Agent.mode initializes Session.mode; missing legacy mode is build.
  Failure before commit exposes no Session ID.
  No MessageEntry, AgentSession or model inference is created.
  The first execution assembles Agent, SYSTEM, Skills and tools.
end note
note over Mate,API
  No If-Match or Idempotency-Key. Each successful POST creates a Session.
  Repeating an uncertain request may create another Session.
  Background cleanup handles unbound orphan Sessions.
end note
note over Resolver,Store
  Target IDs use agent- or session- plus 32 hexadecimal UUID characters.
  Database agent_id must support 38 characters; migrate VARCHAR(30) to 64.
  No execution credentials are consumed; upstream performs authentication.
end note
@enduml

